-- Migration: seed_system_classes_catalog
-- Seed the canonical system_classes catalog (13 classes x {2014, 2024}) so that
-- freshly-migrated databases (CI `supabase start`, preview branches, local
-- `db reset`) have the base class rows. These rows previously lived ONLY in the
-- gitignored supabase/seed.sql (tester dump), so migration-only environments came
-- up with an EMPTY system_classes: the 2024-derivation migrations
-- (20260720000020 / 20260720000037) then ran against an empty source table and
-- inserted nothing, and the pgTAP spellcasting_rules test could not resolve its
-- pinned class definitions (character_classes_definition_pair_check violation).
--
-- Idempotent: ON CONFLICT (ruleset, class_name) DO NOTHING, so production (which
-- already has these rows) is a no-op; a fresh DB gets the full catalog.
-- Pure data migration (canonical class chassis + 2024 compatibility definitions);
-- verbatim snapshot, so its size is intrinsic to the domain.

